Star measurement method (HFD, background, aperture sizing)
---------------------------------------------------------

`TianWen.Lib/Imaging/Image.StarDetection.cs` measures stars by the approach Han
Kleijn documented for ASTAP: a median-plus-MAD background taken from an annulus
outside the aperture, a 3-sigma signal gate, a flux-weighted centroid with the
aperture shrunk until the star is boxed, a radial signal histogram to size the
aperture, and a flux-weighted approximation of the half flux diameter.

  Han Kleijn, ASTAP / HNSKY -- https://www.hnsky.org/astap.htm

The HFD approximation itself is credited by that documentation to Kazuhisa
Miyashita:

  https://astro-limovie.info/occultation_observation/halffluxdiameter/halffluxdiameter_en.html

Further descriptions of the same measurement consulted along the way:

  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half_flux_diameter
  https://www.lost-infinity.com/night-sky-image-processing-part-6-measuring-the-half-flux-diameter-hfd-of-a-star-a-simple-c-implementation/
  http://www.ccdware.com/Files/ITS%20Paper.pdf  (page 10, HFD Measurement Algorithm)

Two parts of that file are deliberately not the published method: FWHM is measured
as an interpolated radial half-maximum crossing rather than the area of the
above-half-maximum samples (see `HalfMaxDiameter`), and ellipticity comes from the
flux-weighted second-moment matrix.

